From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:28:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix: replace fake 4-role BiS data with real per-spec
 Wowhead data (v2.5.0)

GuideData.lua was hand-written with only 4 generic buckets (healer/tank/
melee/caster), so every spec sharing a role saw the exact same item list
regardless of class or weapon type (e.g. Hunters shown a fist weapon,
every melee spec seeing identical gear). GearManager also hard-blocked
any item with ID < 260000, which incorrectly filtered out legitimate
crafted BiS items.

GuideData.lua is now auto-generated by scraper/build-data.js from real
per-class/spec Wowhead bis-gear guides (all 40 specs, including the
previously-missing Devourer Demon Hunter). GearManager no longer
re-guesses armor/weapon type or item-ID range - it trusts the per-spec
source data and derives GetFarmPlan() from each item's own drop source
instead of a small hand-maintained dungeon loot table. Also fixed a
latent bug where Character:GetInventoryUpgrades() called a GearManager
method that never existed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
