From 5339d8bcc82dd704ba078f20901381ed1db3ba30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(ui): modern flat/dark redesign with class-color
 accents (v2.5.0)

Replaces the classic beveled tooltip-border look (tiled ChatFrameBackground,
boxed 3D tab buttons, single-line gold text headers) with a shared theme:

- New Core/Theme.lua: flat hairline-bordered "card" panels, the player's
  class color used as one consistent accent throughout (top accent bar,
  active tab underline, header name, hover highlight, BiS/upgrade tags)
  instead of a static gold everywhere. Pure texture/font code, no bundled
  art assets.
- Main window (Modules/TalentCompare/UI.lua): underline-style tabs instead
  of boxed buttons, a card header with a small item-level badge next to
  the player name, and icon-forward two-line item rows (name on top,
  slot + source as a muted subtitle below) instead of single plain text
  lines - reused across the Dashboard/Farm/Upgrades/BiS tabs. Each tab now
  has a consistent accent-colored title + muted subtitle instead of one
  hand-built, differently-formatted text block per tab.
- AI Coach chat panel (Modules/AICoach/ChatUI.lua): swapped the tiled
  chat-frame background for the same flat panel style; the "Coach:"
  message prefix now uses the class-color accent instead of a hardcoded
  green.

All functional logic (module calls, GearManager data, popups, slash
commands) is unchanged - this is a visual-layer rewrite.

